\f0\fs18 \cf0 Modify Info.plist to include the correct version number.\
\
Copy the SCCube.icns file into Standalone Resources\
\
Change MainMenu.nib to replace references to SuperCollider with BEASTmulch System (app and help menus)\
\
Copy Close from File to Window Menu and set selector. This keeps Cmd-W working\
\
Change Identifier to uk.ac.bham.beast\
\
Follow instructions in Creating-Standalone-Applications, using the name BEASTMulch System.\
	-make sure to select the 'Deployment' build configuration.\
\
Open the bundle by right-clicking and selecting Show Package Contents. Go into resources, where the class library, etc. are.\
\
Copy the contents of build/Help into resources/Help.\
\
Delete resources/Help/Help.help.rtf\
\
Copy scsynth to resources/\
	- to use local server\
	\
Run lib-distro to make a library distribution\
\
Copy in the directories from the UGens folder to plugins/ classlib/ and Help/. A fast way to do this is to just copy them all three times. (SC ignores them as appropriate\
\
Copy the source directory to class library.\
\
Copy Master.rtf to SCClassLibrary\
\
Copy in all required extensions listed in the Dependencies file.\
\
Make a distribution folder, and add the copyright and license file.\
\
Test the standalone thoroughly.\
\
Archive the file as a zip, and add it to BEASTMulch SVN in the tags/Standalones/ dir, in a new directory named day-month-year, filenamed SCrevX-desc.zip where X is the SC code revision, and desc is an optional description, e.g. before-Copenhagen.}